nty"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids, July to August came in under 90% of normal in 41 years, more than any other pair, and it is also the driest pair at 2.67 inches. In 2025, June to July came in at 20% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, April to May sits at 62% of normal on the middle of the grids.</p>"}
